# AI integration boundary

**Binding:** [ADR-007: AI provider contract](../adrs/ADR-007-ai-provider-contract.md) (Accepted), [ADR-006: Serverless and secret boundary](../adrs/ADR-006-serverless-and-secret-boundary.md) (Accepted). **Product context:** [ADR-001](../adrs/ADR-001-product-operating-model.md) (optional AI), [ADR-003](../adrs/ADR-003-ai-suggestion-lifecycle.md) (transient suggestions). **Schemas:** [ADR-008](../adrs/ADR-008-schema-led-domain-contracts.md). **Self-hosting:** [ADR-011](../adrs/ADR-011-self-hosting-provider-model.md) (Accepted).

## Operating context

Core recipe book flows must work **offline** and **without** Supabase or OpenAI once the app shell and local data are present ([ADR-001](../adrs/ADR-001-product-operating-model.md)). **Supabase** (auth, backup, sharing, sync) and **OpenAI** are **optional enhancements**; do not make them **hard prerequisites** for save, edit, search, organize, or restore of locally owned recipes. When AI is unavailable, **degrade** (clear UI, disabled actions) instead of blocking the recipe book ([ADR-001](../adrs/ADR-001-product-operating-model.md), [ADR-007](../adrs/ADR-007-ai-provider-contract.md) offline / no-AI behavior).

For **new or changed AI features**, prefer **Responses API** + **Zod-structured output** under `$lib/api/ai/` ([ADR-007](../adrs/ADR-007-ai-provider-contract.md)); **do not extend** legacy **Chat Completions** in [`src/lib/server/openai.ts`](../src/lib/server/openai.ts) — see **New and changed AI work** below.

## Where AI may run

- **Provider clients and private env** live only in the **server graph**: `+server.ts`, `+page.server.ts` / `+layout.server.ts`, `hooks.server.ts`, and modules **only** imported from those (see ADR-006). The browser calls **same-origin HTTP APIs** under `src/routes/api/**` (or server loads); it does **not** construct `OpenAI` or hold API keys.
- **`src/lib/api/ai/ai.queries.ts`** (and similar) may run in the client: they must **only** call those HTTP endpoints, not import `ai.model.ts` or any module that pulls in the OpenAI SDK or `$env/static/private`.

## New and changed AI work

- **Preferred path:** [Responses API](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/responses) + **Zod-structured output** via `$lib/api/ai` patterns ([`src/lib/api/ai/ai.model.ts`](../src/lib/api/ai/ai.model.ts)). **Do not add** new `chat.completions.create` call sites; legacy usage in [`src/lib/server/openai.ts`](../src/lib/server/openai.ts) is **deprecated** (migrate when touching those flows).
- **Boundaries:** Parse and validate (or reject) provider output **before** returning success to the client. For Responses flows, the Zod schema paired with `zodTextFormat` is authoritative; do not return unvalidated JSON (ADR-007).
- **`zodTextFormat` schemas:** Use **plain JSON-shaped** Zod (objects, arrays, primitives, null where allowed). **`.describe()`** on fields is encouraged; **avoid** **`.transform()`**, **`.pipe()`**, and heavy **`.refine()`** on the **same** schema you pass to `zodTextFormat`—apply those in a **follow-up** `safeParse` or helper after structured output validates (ADR-007).
- **Preferences:** **Recipe idea** and **full recipe from suggestion** flows must pass the caller’s **preferences string** into provider instructions (including empty when none). Other flows should include preferences when they affect dietary or constraint-sensitive output; if not yet wired, record drift in [`docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md`](../docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md) (ADR-007, preference inclusion).
- **Errors:** Map missing key to a **disabled** outcome (`OPENAI_DISABLED` / **503** where established); never leak secrets or raw provider errors (ADR-007, errors and availability).

## Provider-agnostic discipline

- Do not embed **OpenAI-only** assumptions in **shared client types**, route **contracts**, or UI copy where a future **user-configured** or OpenAI-compatible gateway must satisfy the same JSON shapes and server-only config (ADR-007 future user-configured provider; ADR-011). Keep keys and base URLs **server-side only**; avoid barrel files that re-export server AI implementations to client-importable modules (ADR-006).

## Escalation

- Conflicts with Accepted ADRs or intentional contract drift: follow [`.cursor/rules/adr-compliance.mdc`](./adr-compliance.mdc) and [`docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md`](../docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md).
